## Finding

An older Phase 6 audit entry still described shallow `TopicRouteData` clone
identity as an owned-value difference. The pinned Java `TopicRouteData` source
uses `addAll`/`putAll` to allocate new outer collections while sharing nested
DTO/list references. Current Rust `java_copy_constructed` and
`clone_topic_route_data` do the same through shared handles; the deep clone
creates distinct nested handles. The Java fixture records outer and nested
identity flags, and the Protocol differential compares them against Rust
`SharedValue::ptr_eq` checks. The historical caveat was stale, not a current
implementation gap; the audit now states that explicitly.

